      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nFix KV cache allocation with pipeline parallelism when a KV cache group has no layers on one PP stage. DeepSeek-V4 with `-tp 4 -pp 2` fails at startup with `StopIteration`, and the engine reports an empty error message.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- DeepSeek-V4 starts with TP=4, PP=2. Before this change, the PP0 workers crashed during KV cache initialization.\r\n- If a KV cache tensor's layer is in no group, `allocate_kv_cache` now raises a `RuntimeError` naming the layer. Before, it raised `StopIteration`, which has no message, so the engine reported an empty error: `Worker failed with error ''`.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nWith PP, `_project_kv_cache_groups_to_worker` narrows each group's `layer_names` to the stage's own layers. When a group has no layers on a stage, it keeps the original `UniformTypeKVCacheSpecs`, which still lists other stages' layers. `get_kv_cache_config_from_groups` iterated `kv_cache_specs`, so it created tensors for layers the stage does not own. `allocate_kv_cache` then found no group for those layers.\r\n\r\nFix:\r\n\r\n- `vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py`: iterate `group.layer_names` instead of the spec's layers, so empty groups produce no tensors.\r\n- `vllm/v1/worker/utils.py`: raise a `RuntimeError` naming the layer when a tensor's layer is in no group.\r\n\r\nThere is no change when PP=1 or when no stage has an empty group.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nSetup: DeepSeek-V4-Flash truncated to its first 6 layers (local checkpoint), 8x Intel Arc Pro B60 (XPU), `BLHNC` KV cache layout.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nvllm serve DeepSeek-V4-Flash-6L --trust-remote-code \\\r\n  --tensor-parallel-size 4 --pipeline-parallel-size 2 \\\r\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --max-model-len 8192 --max-num-seqs 2 \\\r\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.85\r\n```\r\n\r\nBefore (PP0 workers): the error message is empty because `StopIteration` has no message.\r\n\r\n```text\r\nFile \"vllm/v1/worker/utils.py\", line 432, in allocate_kv_cache\r\n    group_id, group = next(\r\nStopIteration\r\nRuntimeError: Worker failed with error '', please check the stack trace above for the root cause\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter: all 8 workers allocate the KV cache and the server starts. If a tensor's layer is ever outside every group again, the error names the layer instead of being empty (covered by `test_allocate_kv_cache_rejects_tensor_outside_groups`):\r\n\r\n```text\r\nRuntimeError: KV cache tensor layer '<layer_name>' is not in any KV cache group.\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnit tests (`tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py`):\r\n\r\n- `test_get_kv_cache_config_skips_empty_projected_uniform_group`\r\n- `test_allocate_kv_cache_rejects_tensor_outside_groups`\r\n- `test_get_kv_cache_configs_empty_pp_group_replans_to_min_blocks`\r\n\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npytest -v tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py \\\r\n  -k \"empty_projected_uniform_group or rejects_tensor_outside_groups or empty_pp_group\"\r\n```\r\n",
